## Component Conventions

- **Location:** All shared components live in `packages/ui/src/components/`.
- **Barrel export:** Every component is re-exported from `packages/ui/src/index.tsx`.
- **Props:** Accept `className?: string` for NativeWind overrides via the consumer.
- **Naming:** PascalCase filenames matching the component name (e.g., `EventCard.tsx`).
- **Icons (mobile):** Use `@expo/vector-icons` only (Ionicons, Feather, MaterialCommunityIcons). Never import SVGs directly.
- **Icons (web):** Use `react-icons` for parity with mobile. Import from `react-icons/fi` (Feather), `react-icons/io5` (Ionicons), `react-icons/si` (Simple Icons for brand logos e.g. SiInstagram, SiX). Same icon families as mobile — FiCalendar matches Feather calendar, IoLogoInstagram matches Ionicons.
- **Images:** Use the `FlameImage` wrapper (`packages/ui/src/components/FlameImage.tsx`) for remote images. It is built on `expo-image` and provides: (1) 300ms cross-fade transition; (2) `memory-disk` cache policy for aggressive caching; (3) optional `blurhash` placeholder prop; (4) `contentFit` (maps to expo-image's API). Use `source={{ uri }}` for remote URLs. Prefer `FlameImage` over RN `Image` or `ImageBackground` in new code.
- **Font family:** Use custom `fontFamily` tokens: `font-poppins`, `font-poppins-light`, `font-poppins-medium`, `font-poppins-semibold`, `font-poppins-bold`.
- **RefreshControl (pull-to-refresh):** Use `CustomRefreshControl` from `@project-flame/ui`. RN 0.81+ ignores tintColor at mount on iOS (New Architecture); `CustomRefreshControl` works around this by initialising with `"transparent"` then applying `#FFFFFF` after 500ms. The initial value MUST be `"transparent"` — using `"white"` fails because both `"white"` and `"#FFFFFF"` normalise to the same C++ `SharedColor` value, so the bridge skips the update. Do NOT use raw `RefreshControl` — tintColor won't apply. See https://github.com/facebook/react-native/issues/53987. Documented in MARCH_2026_FIXES.md #147, #151–153.
- **ActivityIndicator on dark backgrounds:** Use literal `#FFFFFF` for full-screen or in-content loading spinners on dark screens (bg-background, surface). Do NOT use `colors["white-100"]` (#F9FBFE) — it renders faint. Same rule as RefreshControl.
- **Dark text on light buttons (FlameText gotcha):** `FlameText` has a hardcoded default `text-white-100` class. Passing `text-dark` via className may not reliably override it in NativeWind. For button labels on white/light backgrounds (`bg-white-100`), use raw `<Text>` with `style={{ color: colors.dark }}` instead of `FlameText`. This matches the pattern used by all other buttons in the app. See MARCH_2026_FIXES.md #327.
- **Text inputs and search fields (dark surfaces only):** Use `bg-white-5 border border-white-10` on all text inputs and search bars (pill or card radius depending on context). White-filled inputs (`bg-[#F6F6F6]` / `bg-white-100`) were removed from dark screens because they draw excessive focus and break visual hierarchy. Reference patterns: create-event inputs (`bg-white-5 border border-white-10 rounded-pill p-4`) and `TicketSearchBar`. Placeholder text uses `text-white-50`; input text uses `text-white-100`.

