## Web (Next.js / Tailwind) Conventions

> Source of truth for all Phase 9+ web work. Derived from `docs/prompts/prompts_phases_web_design.md`.

### Goal

The web app **exactly replicates the mobile app's layout, structure, and content** — same sections in the same order, same information displayed, same card layouts, same empty/loading/error states. The only structural differences: web has a persistent top Navbar (no tab bar), and web has a Footer on the home page. Everything else is an exact match to mobile.

**Design source of truth order:**
1. Active mobile screen (`apps/mobile/`) — read this first for any screen
2. `flame-design-system.mdc` — tokens, conventions
3. `packages/ui/tailwind.config.js` — exact token values

### Max-Width Container (all pages, no exceptions)

```html
<div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-4">
  <!-- content -->
</div>
```

Every section on every web page wraps in `max-w-[800px] mx-auto`. Layouts stay single-column — no grid rewrites. This was established in P9 and applies to all future screens.

### FlameText Variant → Web Tailwind Mapping

Mobile uses `<FlameText variant="...">` — always look up the exact web equivalent. **Do NOT guess sizes or weights.**

| Mobile `FlameText` variant | Web Tailwind equivalent                         | Common use                          |
| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| `h3`                       | `text-2xl leading-8 font-poppins-medium`        | Section headers                     |
| `h4`                       | `text-lg font-poppins-semibold`                 | Card titles, event names            |
| `body`                     | `text-base leading-[22px] font-poppins`         | Description text, paragraphs        |
| `subtitle1`                | `text-sm leading-5 font-poppins`                | CTA links, nav labels, org names    |
| `subtitle1-light`          | `text-sm leading-5 font-poppins-light`          | Secondary labels                    |
| `subtitle2`                | `text-xs leading-4 font-poppins-medium`         | Price display, badge text           |
| `subtitle2-light`          | `text-xs leading-4 font-poppins-light`          | Date, time, location metadata       |

> **Common bug:** Using `text-sm font-poppins` for card titles (`h4` = `text-lg font-poppins-semibold`) and using `font-poppins` (400) where `subtitle2-light` needs `font-poppins-light` (300). Caught in P9-3 and P9-4 — do not repeat.

